# AgriVoice — Showcase Build Overview

AgriVoice turns scattered, outdated market gossip into a **real-time, comparable,
confidence-scored crop-price picture** for Ethiopian farmers. The long-term moat
is the **crowd-data loop** — a growing base of real reported sale prices — not the
AI. This build showcases that loop live.

## What we are demoing (the pivot — read this)

The original concept was voice-first (farmer speaks → STT → LLM → TTS). **For this
showcase, voice is PARKED.** Amharic STT is the single most likely thing to fail
on stage, and it isn't what proves the idea. Instead we demo the data engine:

> **The money shot:** a human **agent** enters a farmer's price in the data-entry
> portal, it shows up in the live data list, and the public **dashboard** updates
> in front of the judges — new price, new confidence %, new trend, live on the map.

That one loop proves the crowd-data moat. Everything we build serves it.

## How we divide the work (by functionality, NOT by front/back)

There is **no "frontend person" and no "backend person".** Each teammate owns one
**functionality end-to-end** — its React/Inertia pages AND its Laravel
controllers/services/endpoints. `010`/`020` are shared *conventions* everyone
follows; they are not an ownership split.

| Owner | Functionality (full-stack slice) | Guide |
|-------|----------------------------------|-------|
| **Tsegaye** | **Live dashboard** — the projector screen + the aggregation/confidence/trend engine that feeds it | `100-owner-tsegaye-dashboard.mdc` |
| **Gezachew** | **Data-entry portal** — agent login + entry form + store/validate reports | `110-owner-gezachew-entry-portal.mdc` |
| **Nati** | **Live data list & moderation** — the feed + filters + flag-outlier + its endpoints | `120-owner-nati-live-list.mdc` |
| **Nba** | **Bidding tab** — buyers/sellers post bids (a 2nd crowd data signal) + folding bids into the market picture | `130-owner-nba-bidding.mdc` |

Each person writes their own front and back. The only thing you all touch in
common is the shared foundation below — agree it **day one**.

## Locked decisions (do not re-litigate)

1. **"Live" = polling.** Dashboard, list, and bids re-fetch every ~2–3s via
   Inertia `router.reload({ only: [...] })`. No websockets/Reverb — must survive
   conference wifi.
2. **Named agents, light login.** Each agent has a name + PIN so every entry is
   attributed ("entered by Nati"). Powers attribution + the flag-outlier story.
   No full user auth beyond this.
3. **One host laptop.** The showcase laptop runs Laravel + SQLite and serves the
   dashboard on the projector; everyone else hits the host's LAN IP
   (`http://<host-ip>:8000`). See `050-infra-devops.mdc`.

## Shared foundation (day-one, agreed by all four)

These are the seams between slices. Freeze them before anyone goes deep, so four
people writing four backends don't disagree on the `reports` table or field names.

**Data model** (full schema in `040-database-eloquent.mdc`): `agents`, `markets`,
`reports`, `bids`. `reports` is the shared heart — Gezachew writes its migration,
Tsegaye and Nati read it. Coordinate its columns first.

**The endpoint contract:**
- `POST /reports` — agent submits a price (Gezachew).
- `GET  /reports` — the live list, newest first, with `agentName` (Nati).
- `POST /reports/{id}/flag` — flag an outlier, excluded from aggregates (Nati).
- `GET  /dashboard` (Inertia `snapshots`) — 6 aggregated tiles (Tsegaye).
- `POST /bids` + `GET /bids` — post/list bids (Nba).
- agent login (name + PIN) — sets the session agent (Gezachew).

**Seeding** — collaborative: each owner seeds their own slice's data (Gezachew:
agents + a spread of reports; Nba: sample bids; Tsegaye: market coords). One
`php artisan migrate:fresh --seed` must yield a demo-ready DB. Never live-fetch
during judging.

## Out of scope (say it out loud — nobody builds these)

- Voice pipeline (STT/TTS/LLM). Parked — see `030`. A single canned voice clip is
  an *optional* stretch, never on the critical path.
- Cooperative dashboard, trader/exporter API, NGO reporting, agri-input cross-sell
  — that's the *business model*, not the demo.
- Real user auth/accounts, payments, admin panels, settings pages.
- Any crop or market outside the fixed scope below.

## Fixed scope

- **Crops:** Teff, Coffee (only).
- **Markets:** Adama, Addis Ababa, Jimma (only) — 2 crops × 3 markets = 6 dashboard tiles.
- **Currency/unit:** ETB per quintal, everywhere.

## Stack (authoritative — ignore any Next.js in old planning docs)

- **Backend:** Laravel (PHP 8.2+). **Frontend:** React + TypeScript via **Inertia.js**
  (monolith, pages in `resources/js/Pages/`). **Build:** Vite. **Styling:** Tailwind
  (+ shadcn/ui if the starter has it). **Map:** Leaflet. **DB:** SQLite (single file).
- There is already a starter Laravel + React app in `agrivoice/`. **Extend it** —
  match existing folder layout, naming, and routing. Never import from `next/*`.
